{
  "dom_id": "step-q59919",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "From top to bottom, what are the missing numbers in the ratio table below?\n\n| $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $?$ |\n| $?$ | $30$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $3:5$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($3$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($5$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $12,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 4}{5\\times 4}=\\frac{12}{20}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $30,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 6}{5\\times 6}=\\frac{18}{30}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $20$ |\n| $18$ | $30$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the missing numbers are $20$ and $18.$",
